{"name":"Epsom","hex":"#829161","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Epsom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in Epsom and Ewell borough, Surrey, England, known for its racecourse .","An unincorporated community in Bogard Township, Daviess County, Indiana, United States; the well water tasted of Epsom salts."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Epsom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Epsom","blocks":[{"text":"Epsom is a town in the borough of Epsom and Ewell in Surrey, England, about 14 miles south of central London. The town is first recorded as Ebesham in the 10th century and its name probably derives from that of a Saxon landowner. The earliest evidence of human activity is from the mid-Bronze Age, but the modern settlement probably grew up in the area surrounding St Martin's Church in the 6th or 7th centuries and the street pattern is thought to have become established in the Middle Ages. Today the High Street is dominated by the clock tower, which was erected in 1847–8."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Spring_in_Epsom_%286980024124%29_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Spring_in_Epsom_%286980024124%29_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epsom","wikidata":"Q993164"},{"title":"Epsom (New Zealand electorate)","blocks":[{"text":"Epsom is a New Zealand electorate in Auckland, returning one Member of Parliament to the New Zealand House of Representatives. Since the 2014 general election, Epsom has been represented by David Seymour, the leader of the ACT Party."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Epsom_2026_electorate_boundaries.svg/330px-Epsom_2026_electorate_boundaries.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epsom_(New_Zealand_electorate)","wikidata":"Q5383983"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or